{"report_id":"R0001","domain":"D02","judgment":"PARTIAL","rationale":"Formulation defines partition, resource, and delay/energy constraints, but §II.E fixes ES selection to the closest ES despite §II.D's objective, and limit values are not specified.","locators":[{"page":2,"section":"II.D","quote":"Constraint (C3) declares the range of the partition points. (C4) illustrates the limited delay and energy consumption"},{"page":2,"section":"II.E","quote":"select the ES closest to the UAV."},{"page":3,"section":"III.A","quote":null}]}
{"report_id":"R0002","domain":"D03","judgment":"PARTIAL","rationale":"Topology, workload, and platform parameters are reported in §VII.A and Fig. 2(b), but LST-GNN training details, window length Y, prediction thresholds, and simulator software are omitted.","locators":[{"page":5,"section":"IV.B","quote":"within a historical window of length Y."},{"page":7,"section":"VII.A","quote":"the real-world UAV platform and parameter configurations are shown in Fig. 2."},{"page":7,"section":"VII.A","quote":"a ResNet-18 model trained on the CIFAR-10 dataset is adopted for image classification."},{"page":7,"section":"VII.A (Fig. 2(b))","quote":null}]}
{"report_id":"R0002","domain":"D09","judgment":"NOT_REPORTED","rationale":"Inspected §VII.A, §VIII, and end matter for author code, simulation scripts, traces, or trained-model releases; only public CIFAR-10 use is mentioned, with no author-released artifacts reported.","locators":[{"page":7,"section":"VII.A","quote":"a ResNet-18 model trained on the CIFAR-10 dataset is adopted for image classification."},{"page":9,"section":"VIII and end matter","quote":null}]}
{"report_id":"R0003","domain":"D07","judgment":"PARTIAL","rationale":"Trace-driven simulation uses real-world UAV trajectory traces, but assumes centralized global knowledge of trajectories, channels, and tasks at U1 and lacks physical flight validation.","locators":[{"page":2,"section":"III","quote":"has the information of all the UAVs' trajectories, channel conditions, and inference task distributions."},{"page":5,"section":"V.A","quote":"the trajectories of the UAVs in our simulation are based on the real-world trajectory traces obtained from [21]."}]}
{"report_id":"R0006","domain":"D08","judgment":"PARTIAL","rationale":"Observed critical-area coverage plateaus at a partial level that meets the spatial constraint, so the same paragraph's claim of complete monitoring coverage overstates the reported coverage.","locators":[{"page":6,"section":"V.B","quote":"stabilizes at 87.0%, indicating that AirInfer effectively adheres to spatial constraints."},{"page":6,"section":"V.B","quote":"critical area coverage substantially increased from 47.0% to 87.0%. This confirms AirInfer's effectiveness in achieving complete monitoring coverage."}]}
{"report_id":"R0009","domain":"D05","judgment":"YES","rationale":"Objective minimizes weighted system latency and energy consumption, and evaluation directly reports cumulative rewards alongside total energy consumption and average task latency across test conditions.","locators":[{"page":4,"section":"III","quote":"We aim to minimize the system's weighted latency and energy consumption"},{"page":8,"section":"V.B","quote":"Fig. 4. The cumulative rewards versus time slots."},{"page":9,"section":"V.B","quote":"Fig. 5. The total energy consumption and average task latency versus coverage radius size of UAVs."}]}
